(1) Any dispute about the mode of trial shall be resolved in a summary manner, relying on (a) the pleadings, (b) statements by the parties of the issues to be resolved at the streamlined trial, (c) outlines of the evidence that would be called at the streamlined trial, and (d) other relevant information, if any.
(2) If the case conference judge or trial judge concludes that an objection to the use of the streamlined trial was unjustified, the case conference judge or trial judge, as the case may be, may do one or more of the following:
(a) make a procedural order;
(b) make a costs award for costs incurred as a result of the objection;
(c) impose a penalty under rule 10.49.

*[Alta. Reg. 126/2023, s. 11 effective January 1, 2024 (Alta. Gaz. November 30, 2023)]*
